cff-version: 1.2.0
title: "fyndling-mcp - MCP server for medieval events, places and historical recipes"
message: "If you use this software or its data, please cite it as below."
type: software
authors:
  - given-names: "Ralf René"
    family-names: "Vitasek"
    orcid: "https://orcid.org/0009-0007-4677-5679"
    affiliation: "Fyndling.de"
abstract: >-
  Model Context Protocol (MCP) server for Fyndling.de. It gives AI clients
  access to medieval markets and living-history events in Europe and North
  America, permanent places (meaderies, castles, medieval restaurants) and a
  corpus of historical recipes (c. 1300-1695) with transcriptions, modern
  adaptations and structured ingredient lists. Endpoint:
  https://fyndling.de/mcp (Streamable HTTP, no authentication).
url: "https://fyndling.de"
repository-code: "https://github.com/neongrau/fyndling-mcp"
keywords:
  - "Model Context Protocol"
  - "MCP"
  - "medieval markets"
  - "living history"
  - "historical recipes"
  - "culinary history"
license: CC0-1.0
